WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.406
Insidious is known for creeping out its audience with horrors, hiding in plain sight, 

00:00:03.428 --> 00:00:06.686
whether it be this creepy face on the bathroom mirror in the opening credits, 

00:00:06.708 --> 00:00:10.206
or the ghost of this boy blending into the laundry room as

00:00:10.228 --> 00:00:11.870
Renai cleans up around the new house.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.926
But there are also clues about the film's ending, connections to other

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:18.234
horror films by director James Wan and Blumhouse Easter eggs.

00:00:18.282 --> 00:00:21.742
To learn why Specs uses raw steak to ice his head instead of an ice pack,

00:00:21.796 --> 00:00:23.370
and other Insidious secrets.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.800
Stick around to the end of the this video.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.918
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:00:30.918 --> 00:00:35.042
There are some horror movie details that are beyond our perception,

00:00:35.106 --> 00:00:37.126
beyond our understanding from the physical world.

00:00:37.228 --> 00:00:40.646
But there is another plane of existence, an infinite realm, where these

00:00:40.668 --> 00:00:45.478
details are collected and analyzed by a mysterious entity with a goatee.

00:00:45.574 --> 00:00:46.778
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:00:46.864 --> 00:00:50.646
Director James Wan is most known for his work in the horror genre.

00:00:50.678 --> 00:00:54.186
Saw, Dead Silence, The Conjuring films, Malignant. I have been covering all of his horror

00:00:54.218 --> 00:00:57.086
films here on Things You Missed, but there is one that I've been saving

00:00:57.188 --> 00:00:58.286
until now.

00:00:58.388 --> 00:01:01.466
In this episode, I'll be covering Stygian.

00:01:01.578 --> 00:01:02.154
Just kidding.

00:01:02.202 --> 00:01:02.830
That's not available.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.066
So instead, we'll be stepping into the world of the Further to analyze his

00:01:06.088 --> 00:01:08.126
2010 film, Insidious.

00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:14.910
-[Elise] There are other entities who are malevolent and have a more insidious agenda.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:18.814
This was a formative movie for my taste in the supernatural genre.

00:01:18.862 --> 00:01:22.006
It was the third team up between Juan and screenwriter Leigh Whannell, and the

00:01:22.028 --> 00:01:24.966
second film where Whannell would also play a substantial character in the movie. 

00:01:24.988 --> 00:01:28.166
These two love to hide Easter eggs for the fans, but before we get

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:31.658
into those, let's go back to the beginning to look at a few other

00:01:31.664 --> 00:01:32.730
Things You Might Have Missed.

00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:35.951
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.742
The opening credits are a clue about the midpoint twist.

00:01:38.806 --> 00:01:42.202
At first, Insidious appears to be another haunted house or poltergeist type

00:01:42.256 --> 00:01:45.518
film. But when Elise Rainier is introduced, we learn the reason behind the

00:01:45.524 --> 00:01:46.682
appearance of these ghosts.

00:01:46.746 --> 00:01:50.042
They're trying to possess Dalton because he's left his physical body vacant

00:01:50.106 --> 00:01:51.114
during astral projection.

00:01:51.162 --> 00:01:54.394
The opening title sequence shows the ethereal spirits of the text floating

00:01:54.442 --> 00:01:55.402
up and disappearing.

00:01:55.466 --> 00:01:58.546
When I covered Malignant, I also pointed out how the way the credits are

00:01:58.568 --> 00:02:00.462
animated ties into a plot twist.

00:02:00.526 --> 00:02:03.886
Elise refers to the out of body experiences that Dalton has as astral

00:02:03.918 --> 00:02:06.414
projection, but the word astral has two meanings.

00:02:06.462 --> 00:02:09.358
It's used to refer to something like the Further, which is on another plane

00:02:09.374 --> 00:02:12.642
of existence, but it's also used to refer to something related to the stars.

00:02:12.706 --> 00:02:15.654
When the term was first coined in the 1600s, they were basically one

00:02:15.692 --> 00:02:16.192
and the same

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.622
because space travel was as an obscure of a concept, as traveling to another

00:02:19.676 --> 00:02:20.870
dimension is for us today.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.274
There are a bunch of references to space travel before we learn about astral projection in Insidious. 

00:02:24.322 --> 00:02:27.554
Dalton sleeps under a solar system mobile,

00:02:27.602 --> 00:02:31.198
he draws pictures of himself flying up into space, he a solar system model on

00:02:31.204 --> 00:02:34.686
his dresser, and he has an alien poster in his room that says,

00:02:34.708 --> 00:02:35.870
music, from beyond your little world.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.554
And in his brother's room, there's a whiteboard that says he has a science

00:02:38.602 --> 00:02:40.110
project to due on the solar system.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.102
I have no idea how he's able to reach that whiteboard, but it's a nice idea nonetheless.

00:02:43.156 --> 00:02:46.558
Also, when Josh Lambert goes into the Further, you can spot a

00:02:46.564 --> 00:02:49.418
man reading a newspaper which says something about Starline.

00:02:49.514 --> 00:02:51.150
It's very difficult to make out.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:53.934
There are also other instances of foreshadowing right from the very beginning.

00:02:53.972 --> 00:02:57.058
When we first meet Dalton, he comes downstairs because he doesn't

00:02:57.074 --> 00:02:57.702
like his room.

00:02:57.756 --> 00:03:00.326
This is probably because he's seen the Red Face Demon or one of the other

00:03:00.348 --> 00:03:02.022
spirits there, and it frightened him.

00:03:02.076 --> 00:03:04.758
His mom, Renai, is flipping through a photo album, and he asked to see a

00:03:04.764 --> 00:03:07.110
picture of his dad as a kid, but they don't have any.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.694
This is teased again with this line from Josh's mom,

00:03:10.732 --> 00:03:12.578
-[Lorraine] I can't believe you got Josh to hold still for a photo.

00:03:12.674 --> 00:03:16.038
This is all because Josh has a subconscious fear of being photographed due

00:03:16.054 --> 00:03:19.098
to his experience with the Bride in Black appearing behind him in photos as a kid.

00:03:19.104 --> 00:03:21.900
Which Elise had to hypnotize him into forgetting about.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:28.014
-[Elise] I advised Lorraine to hide them, to stop taking your picture, 

00:03:28.052 --> 00:03:28.746
-[Elise] to just let you forget.

00:03:28.858 --> 00:03:31.642
However, I do think Lorraine's line is a little ridiculous.

00:03:31.706 --> 00:03:33.818
It's not like Josh hasn't been in wedding photos.

00:03:33.914 --> 00:03:37.298
There is a nice touch near the end, however, when Josh first enters the Further.

00:03:37.304 --> 00:03:39.710
He's guided by a younger version of himself.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.734
But because he has no photos from his childhood, he doesn't recognize

00:03:42.782 --> 00:03:44.862
himself and momentarily thinks that it's Dalton.

00:03:44.926 --> 00:03:48.446
At first, Josh doesn't even believe Elise about the whole astral projection theory.

00:03:48.478 --> 00:03:52.086
It's not until he realizes that Dalton's drawings match up with what

00:03:52.108 --> 00:03:53.874
she's saying that he becomes convinced.

00:03:53.922 --> 00:03:56.834
We can see these drawings way back at the beginning, including Dalton

00:03:56.882 --> 00:04:00.486
watching himself sleep, a series of red doors which serve as portals in the

00:04:00.508 --> 00:04:02.614
Further, and even the Red Face Demon itself.

00:04:02.732 --> 00:04:05.626
And speaking of red doors, they seem to play a significant part in the way

00:04:05.648 --> 00:04:06.502
the film is shot.

00:04:06.566 --> 00:04:09.754
The camera is constantly traveling through open doors or looking through

00:04:09.792 --> 00:04:11.050
open doors in the real world.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.786
I believe this is to highlight the difference between the real world and the Further.

00:04:13.808 --> 00:04:17.406
The real world is bright and open and while this film doesn't have

00:04:17.428 --> 00:04:20.526
a very vibrant color palette par for the course for late-2000s to

00:04:20.548 --> 00:04:23.994
early-2010s PG-13 horror, the scenes in the real world feel more colorful

00:04:24.042 --> 00:04:27.086
when compared to the literal monotony of the scenes in the Further which are

00:04:27.108 --> 00:04:27.962
blue or red.

00:04:28.036 --> 00:04:31.454
I feel like we can come up with a better name for this look than Twilightcore.

00:04:31.502 --> 00:04:34.514
It's not just the look of these films that's iconic, though.

00:04:34.552 --> 00:04:37.806
It's also the sound which plays a part in delivering some incredible jump scares.

00:04:37.838 --> 00:04:40.566
Part of what makes the jump so effective in this movie is that

00:04:40.588 --> 00:04:43.026
Leigh Whannell avoided writing any false jump scares.

00:04:43.058 --> 00:04:46.614
There are no loud noises to accompany moments when it's just the cat or just

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:47.890
some kids playing a prank.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:51.082
Composer Joseph Bishara created a lot of stingers that sound like someone

00:04:51.136 --> 00:04:52.490
banging on a piano.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:54.605
-[Renai] Dalton...

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:58.138
And this feels significant because Renai is a pianist who writes songs for

00:04:58.144 --> 00:04:58.710
her husband.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:02.246
The same instrument is used for Renai to express her love and the evil

00:05:02.278 --> 00:05:03.722
nature of the ghosts around her.

00:05:03.776 --> 00:05:06.974
James Wan is really good at finding creative ways to illustrate the whole

00:05:07.012 --> 00:05:09.082
compare and contrast thing between the two worlds.

00:05:09.146 --> 00:05:12.078
For example, the movie begins when we transition from the opening credits to

00:05:12.084 --> 00:05:15.134
a shot of Renai laying in bed, where we fade from black and white into color.

00:05:15.172 --> 00:05:18.498
It foreshadows the ending where Dalton makes it back to his body, and

00:05:18.504 --> 00:05:21.314
we fade from the aesthetic of the further back to the colors of the real world.

00:05:21.352 --> 00:05:23.054
Josh is a history teacher.

00:05:23.102 --> 00:05:25.566
There's just something interesting about a history teacher who doesn't

00:05:25.598 --> 00:05:26.882
remember his own past.

00:05:27.016 --> 00:05:29.502
Speaking of which, there are a ton of Easter eggs in his classroom.

00:05:29.566 --> 00:05:32.118
The first time we visit it, there's a list of students who have detention on

00:05:32.124 --> 00:05:32.754
the chalkboard.

00:05:32.802 --> 00:05:36.066
The first is Joe Hui, the craft service provider listed in the movie's credits.

00:05:36.098 --> 00:05:39.266
Heather Mitchell was a set dresser, Lisa Cabello was a craft services

00:05:39.298 --> 00:05:42.374
production assistant, and Kaylee Fisher was another set dresser.

00:05:42.422 --> 00:05:45.238
James Wan, the director, apparently has double detention.

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:48.698
Yesim Osman was the head of the hair department and Leslie Borchard was a hairstylist.

00:05:48.704 --> 00:05:51.898
Underneath that, there's a sketch of Billy the puppet from the

00:05:51.904 --> 00:05:52.678
Saw movies.

00:05:52.774 --> 00:05:56.046
Billy used to have a little cameo in every James Wan movie, and at the time

00:05:56.068 --> 00:05:59.086
of writing, this Insidious Easter egg would be the last example.

00:05:59.188 --> 00:06:02.318
However, I'm sure he'll appear again in the future, and he has shown up in a

00:06:02.324 --> 00:06:04.010
couple of Leigh Whannell directed films.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.102
But this appearance on the chalkboard is the most significant one of all.

00:06:07.156 --> 00:06:10.626
Insidious technically first played in 2010, but it got its wide release in 2011,

00:06:10.648 --> 00:06:14.270
a year after Saw VII, which was dubbed The Final Chapter.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.454
So the Saw series was considered to be over by the time the Insidious

00:06:17.502 --> 00:06:18.350
franchise began.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:21.318
Underneath the chalkboard drawing, you'll notice the number eight, which at

00:06:21.324 --> 00:06:25.302
the time was our only clue about a possible revival and 8th movie in the Saw

00:06:25.356 --> 00:06:29.266
franchise. We would eventually get that movie with Jigsaw in 2017.

00:06:29.378 --> 00:06:32.294
On another day, there's another scene of Josh staying back in the classroom,

00:06:32.342 --> 00:06:34.374
and there are even more crew reference Easter eggs.

00:06:34.422 --> 00:06:37.846
That day's round of detentions includes Rick Osako, who's the unit production manager,

00:06:37.878 --> 00:06:41.834
Jeanette Brill, the line producer Jen Spencer, which is pretty close

00:06:41.872 --> 00:06:45.898
to Jennifer Spence, the art director, Kate Mallor, a set dresser,

00:06:45.914 --> 00:06:47.514
and Renetta Amador, the script supervisor.

00:06:47.562 --> 00:06:50.794
There's one other sort of crew reference connection Leigh Winnell's wife,

00:06:50.842 --> 00:06:52.714
Corbett Tuck has two roles in the film.

00:06:52.762 --> 00:06:55.822
She's one of the nurses and doll girl number two in the Further.

00:06:55.886 --> 00:06:58.606
The Billy the puppet drawing on the chalkboard was not the only connection

00:06:58.638 --> 00:06:59.374
to James Wan.

00:06:59.422 --> 00:07:03.570
Insidious also helped set the stage for one of his future franchises.

00:07:03.877 --> 00:07:06.990
(Impact)

00:07:08.823 --> 00:07:12.455
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:15.954
In my various Things You Missed videos on the horror films of James Wan,

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:18.486
there have been a number of recurring elements that I've identified that

00:07:18.508 --> 00:07:22.134
make Wan an auteur, or a director with a distinctive approach, making him

00:07:22.172 --> 00:07:24.102
recognizable as the author of the movie.

00:07:24.166 --> 00:07:27.306
For example, the film begins with the Labbert family moving in, and they end

00:07:27.328 --> 00:07:29.242
up moving again before it's all said and done.

00:07:29.296 --> 00:07:32.746
Dead Silence and The Conjuring both feature protagonists who move to a new house.

00:07:32.768 --> 00:07:35.946
I've also talked about several of those films that feature spiraling

00:07:35.978 --> 00:07:38.762
camera movements like Saw, Dead Silence and Malignant.

00:07:38.826 --> 00:07:41.854
Insidious features something similar when Renai looks up at the noise coming

00:07:41.892 --> 00:07:42.830
from the baby's room.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.286
The film also begins with a shot that inverts 180 degrees, which could be

00:07:46.308 --> 00:07:48.910
used to signify the change from the real world to the Further.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:51.886
The Conjuring would do something similar when its protagonist,

00:07:51.918 --> 00:07:54.382
Lorraine Warren, walks to and from the basement housing the witch.

00:07:54.446 --> 00:07:57.138
She's essentially going from a normal place to an evil one.

00:07:57.224 --> 00:08:00.534
In fact, I think James Wan originally wanted to make the conjuring instead

00:08:00.572 --> 00:08:01.330
of Insidious.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.246
The rules of this world are pretty similar to The Conjuring, and the

00:08:04.268 --> 00:08:07.334
grandmother is even named Lorraine, and she's revealed to also have some

00:08:07.372 --> 00:08:08.466
abilities as a traveler.

00:08:08.498 --> 00:08:11.119
I almost wonder if he wanted to make The Conjuring but couldn't get the

00:08:11.119 --> 00:08:13.046
rights until after making Insidious.

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:16.538
This idea is further backed up by The Conjuring Two, which features an

00:08:16.544 --> 00:08:19.638
astral projection scene in the opening, very similar to the Further.

00:08:19.734 --> 00:08:21.430
Personally, I prefer Insidious.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:24.598
The main difference seems to be that the Insidious lore is made up with its

00:08:24.624 --> 00:08:28.158
villains being based on creepy, uncanny valley ideas that James and Leigh had

00:08:28.164 --> 00:08:31.194
been saving up, whereas The Conjuring tends to base its lore on religious

00:08:31.242 --> 00:08:32.394
stuff in urban legends.

00:08:32.442 --> 00:08:35.278
There is one aspect of The Conjuring I like better though, I think it does a

00:08:35.284 --> 00:08:37.742
better job of fleshing out the backstories of the ghosts.

00:08:37.806 --> 00:08:41.070
Another common element in James Wan films is puppets or dolls.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:43.458
Of course, there's the previously mentioned puppet from Saw.

00:08:43.544 --> 00:08:46.674
Dead Silence is all about puppets, and The Conjuring introduces the doll

00:08:46.712 --> 00:08:49.934
Annabelle, who is also briefly in The Conjuring Two and Aquaman.

00:08:49.982 --> 00:08:52.738
In Insidious, there's a moment where we see the inside of the

00:08:52.754 --> 00:08:54.962
Red Face Demon's lair, and it's filled with marionettes.

00:08:55.026 --> 00:08:58.198
Not only is this another example of a puppet, but within this movie it

00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:00.470
symbolizes how the demon controls Dalton's body.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.642
He's essentially moving him around like a puppet.

00:09:02.706 --> 00:09:05.738
When Josh finds Dalton captive in the demon's lair, he's chained at the

00:09:05.744 --> 00:09:07.866
ankles, which has got to be a callback to Saw.

00:09:07.968 --> 00:09:09.914
Another item we've seen time and time again.

00:09:09.952 --> 00:09:11.302
In Juan's work is mannequins.

00:09:11.366 --> 00:09:14.846
They were used at the factory in Saw multiple times in Dead Silence, at

00:09:14.868 --> 00:09:18.238
Parker's house in Insidious chapter two, and in the Amityville basement in

00:09:18.244 --> 00:09:19.070
the Conjuring Two.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:22.638
It's barely noticeable, but I did spot a mannequin in the Lambert's attic at

00:09:22.644 --> 00:09:23.978
the first house in Insidious.

00:09:24.074 --> 00:09:27.346
The door to the demonic layer in The Further is basked in red light.

00:09:27.448 --> 00:09:30.626
This deep red color, in contrast to the blue hues of The Further, is

00:09:30.648 --> 00:09:32.094
inspired by Giallo films.

00:09:32.142 --> 00:09:36.258
Giallo is an Italian genre of mystery / thriller / horror stories, primarily in the

00:09:36.264 --> 00:09:40.098
60s and 70s, which often portrayed a clash of red and blue neon light. 

00:09:40.194 --> 00:09:46.274
-[Leigh] We were inspired by filmmakers like Dario Argento, who take a very operatic approach.

00:09:46.322 --> 00:09:49.798
-[James] Red and black are my color palettes that I love.

00:09:49.884 --> 00:09:54.538
-[James] It really adds to the psychology of the film, and I really wanted the color

00:09:54.624 --> 00:09:57.862
-[James] red to represent the evil in the movie.

00:09:57.926 --> 00:10:01.782
James loves Giallo and has featured intense neon lights in many of his films,

00:10:01.846 --> 00:10:03.850
primarily Dead Silence and Malignant.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:07.466
The Further presented him with an opportunity to really exaggerate the Giallo lighting.

00:10:07.498 --> 00:10:11.166
The metronome that Elise uses to hypnotize Josh also appears to be

00:10:11.188 --> 00:10:13.678
an Italian product, so that may be a part of it.

00:10:13.764 --> 00:10:16.834
Speaking of that scene, the phrases that she used to hypnotize him are taken

00:10:16.872 --> 00:10:21.122
from the Chinese philosopher Laozi: the universe is deathless because having

00:10:21.176 --> 00:10:23.470
no finite self, it stays infinite.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:27.758
A sound man, by not advancing himself, stays the further ahead of himself,

00:10:27.854 --> 00:10:32.146
by not confining himself to himself, sustains himself outside himself.

00:10:32.258 --> 00:10:35.318
Originally, it seems the movie was going to open with this text because it

00:10:35.324 --> 00:10:37.090
can be seen at the beginning of the script.

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:40.406
If you're a longtime fan of paranormal horror, you probably noticed a lot of

00:10:40.428 --> 00:10:43.318
similarities to the 1982 classic Poltergeist.

00:10:43.414 --> 00:10:47.146
Insidious is borderline a remake of this movie, a much more welcome one than

00:10:47.168 --> 00:10:48.310
the actual remake.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:50.474
They both open with the shot of the mom laying in bed.

00:10:50.512 --> 00:10:53.626
They both feature a family of five with one of the young children getting

00:10:53.648 --> 00:10:55.258
trapped in another plane of existence.

00:10:55.354 --> 00:10:58.846
Both families call in a team of three paranormal investigators, but in

00:10:58.868 --> 00:11:02.078
Poltergeist one of them quits and is replaced by an actual psychic, who is a

00:11:02.084 --> 00:11:03.418
better equivalent of Elise.

00:11:03.514 --> 00:11:06.650
In Poltergeist, the psychic explains that the other spirits are hungry for

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:10.258
the child's life force, whereas in Insidious, the psychic explains that the

00:11:10.264 --> 00:11:13.602
spirits can smell his physical vessels available and want to possess him.

00:11:13.656 --> 00:11:16.402
Both movies feature a scene where the family communicates with their child

00:11:16.456 --> 00:11:18.562
and learns that there is a malicious entity after them.

00:11:18.616 --> 00:11:21.606
Both movies have a climactic scene where one of the parents ventures into

00:11:21.628 --> 00:11:23.350
the other world to rescue their kid.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:26.806
In Poltergeist, one of the investigators sees a steak sliding across the

00:11:26.828 --> 00:11:30.486
kitchen countertop all on its own, and perhaps as an homage, when Specs gets

00:11:30.508 --> 00:11:33.914
injured after being Air Yeeted into the wall, he ices his head with a couple

00:11:33.952 --> 00:11:37.062
of raw steaks, one of which sits directly on the kitchen counter.

00:11:37.126 --> 00:11:40.234
When I was rewatching Poltergeist to make this video, I also noticed another

00:11:40.272 --> 00:11:41.722
fun similarity between the two.

00:11:41.776 --> 00:11:44.798
There's a crew member who actually worked on both movies, and it's the

00:11:44.804 --> 00:11:47.194
cinematographer of Insidious, John Leonetti.

00:11:47.242 --> 00:11:50.366
He was the first assistant to the camera operator for Poltergeist, which was

00:11:50.388 --> 00:11:52.622
only the second major movie set he ever worked on.

00:11:52.676 --> 00:11:55.818
As I mentioned, the evil entities in this franchise tend to take advantage

00:11:55.834 --> 00:11:58.974
of the uncanny valley effect, which is when we get creeped out by something

00:11:59.012 --> 00:12:01.118
that seems human but isn't quite human.

00:12:01.204 --> 00:12:04.362
I think this also extends to other things that are not quite as they seem.

00:12:04.426 --> 00:12:07.654
For example, the ghost boy that messes with Renai is actually a short man

00:12:07.692 --> 00:12:10.918
dressed like a boy, and the bride in black is actually a man dressed as a woman.

00:12:10.924 --> 00:12:14.086
The same can be said when we see this mysterious shadow near the

00:12:14.108 --> 00:12:17.238
stairs during the opening credits, or when Josh runs up the stairs in the

00:12:17.244 --> 00:12:20.418
middle of the night in daylight is momentarily pouring through the windows.

00:12:20.514 --> 00:12:21.970
Okay, maybe that one's a mistake.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:25.046
But the choice to make the Bride in Black, a man in woman's clothing is

00:12:25.068 --> 00:12:28.162
expanded upon by giving the character a backstory in the sequel.

00:12:28.226 --> 00:12:31.386
So join me in the next episode of Things You Missed, where I'll be covering

00:12:31.418 --> 00:12:32.782
Insidious Chapter Two.

00:12:32.836 --> 00:12:34.398
You'll find that video on the left.

00:12:34.484 --> 00:12:37.582
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:12:37.636 --> 00:12:41.246
Ring the death bell and select all notifications, and I'll see you in the

00:12:41.268 --> 00:12:43.610
next one, assuming we both survive.

